@startuml
title VDT v0.1 - Evidence upload: physical path and final gate
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
actor Browser
participant "Reverse proxy\nTLS boundary" as Proxy
participant "VDT Policy gate\nsession + scope + expiry" as Gate
participant "Evidence intake" as Intake
participant "Protected filesystem\nquarantine / objects" as Store
database "PostgreSQL\nmetadata + audit" as DB
Browser -> Proxy : POST /api/v1/evidence-items/{id}/evidence-revisions\nmultipart + CSRF + Idempotency-Key + If-Match
Proxy -> Gate : bounded request; trusted forwarding only
Gate -> DB : current principal, scope, assignment, expiry
alt denied
  Gate -> DB : safe denial audit
  Gate --> Proxy : deny; no evidence content
  Proxy --> Browser : 401 / 403 / non-disclosing 404
else allowed initially
  Gate -> Intake : authorized intent (must recheck before commit)
  Intake -> Store : bounded stream to quarantine; server SHA-256
  Intake -> Intake : metadata + MIME + hash + scan validation
  alt incomplete / unsafe / scanner unavailable
    Intake -> DB : operation failure + safe audit
    Intake --> Gate : error; no usable revision
  else validation passed
    Intake -> DB : short transaction: immutable revision\n+ storage STAGED + operation
    Intake -> Store : fsync; atomic rename on same filesystem
    Intake -> Gate : final commit check
    Gate -> DB : lock auth guard + item; recheck time/rights/versions
    alt expired / revoked / version changed
      Gate -> DB : deny/conflict; keep STAGED for safe recovery
      Gate --> Intake : do not publish; orphan lifecycle
    else final gate allowed
      Intake -> DB : atomic COMMITTED + item head/version\n+ audit + idempotency result
      DB --> Intake : commit confirmed
      Intake --> Gate : 201; revision still UNVERIFIED
    end
  end
  Gate --> Proxy : response through reverse proxy
  Proxy --> Browser : result or retryable error
end
note over Intake,DB
File persistence and DB commit are separate.
Crash recovery never publishes using stale authorization.
No assessment consumes a STAGED revision.
end note
@enduml
